It is the next day at the office.
I am sitting next to our software tester.
He looks at the new screens.
He clicks very fast with the mouse.
Suddenly he stops.
He has already found a small mistake.
He looks at me and laughs a little.
"My job is to break things," he says.
"I have to find the mistakes before our users."
He has worked as a tester for five years.
He has tested many different projects.
That is why he finds the problems so fast.
I look at the mistake on my computer.
Fortunately, it is only a small problem.
I fix the code right away.
He tests the program one more time.
Now everything works absolutely perfectly.
I am very glad for his help.
